cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "humanoid-fall-safety-bench: an open benchmark for containment failure in embodied AI agents"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/damvanvi/humanoid-fall-safety-bench"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dam"
    given-names: "Van Vi"
    affiliation: "BivectorAI"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6039-0989"
abstract: >-
  Open, deterministic MuJoCo benchmark that measures the physical consequences
  of naive containment actions (instant Safe Torque Off and instant joint-brake
  lock) on a dynamically balanced humanoid when its high-level AI policy hangs
  or its power or actuators fault. Includes three seeded fault scenarios, a
  no-containment reference arm, a physical impact oracle (fall verdict, head and
  torso impact velocity, kinetic energy at ground contact, time-to-fall) and
  SHA-256 provenance for every trajectory.
keywords:
  - AI control
  - AI safety
  - embodied AI
  - humanoid robots
  - kill switch
  - containment
  - benchmark
  - MuJoCo
  - fall safety
  - reproducibility
